# Current generator scope

The maintained data-generation path is the continuous sputter/PVD likelihood
corpus in `configs/continuous_odf_sputter_pvd_broad.json`. It simulates
film-normal fiber and biaxial growth motifs, with an explicit uniform channel
for nanocrystalline or early-growth texture. See
[continuous_odf_dataset.md](continuous_odf_dataset.md) for commands and
[scientific_texture_space.md](scientific_texture_space.md) for the model.

The repository preserves lower-level texture classes and historical sampling
modes for comparison and reproducibility, but they are not maintained dataset
presets. New corpora should be written below `datasets/`; that location and all
standard generated artifacts are ignored by Git.

The diffraction renderer remains a simulator-development tool, not a
calibrated experimental forward model. Quantitative inference requires
sample-specific validation of structure factors, HCP/low-symmetry geometry,
detector response, backgrounds, counting noise, and microstructure nuisance
parameters. Interpret simulated posterior results as conditional on the
declared generator distribution.
